  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The losing cluster is primarily driven by morning exhaustion whipsaws (10:15\u201311:05 IST) where tight 0.45% stops were systematically hunted within 5 to 90 minutes on counter-trend pullbacks (e.g., TATASTEEL, NTPC, AXISBANK). Furthermore, late-session entries after 14:20 IST (COALINDIA, ICICIBANK) and premature 1.0R trailing breakeven triggers (Trade #7 on AXISBANK) generated gross-positive or near-flat trades that flipped into net losses due to severe transaction fee drag (\u20b944.35 in fees eclipsing the \u20b9-30.23 net P&L).",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE cash equities on a \u20b910,000 micro-capital base, fixed statutory and brokerage costs create an asymmetric hurdle where tight 0.45% stop-losses sit directly inside standard 5-minute retail liquidity sweep noise, requiring wider structural breathing room and higher volume conviction to ensure moves clear the fee threshold.",
