      "min_target_pct": 1.4,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.35,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.25,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.58
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #77 Post-Mortem & Parameter Mutation\nOut-of-sample evaluation revealed severe fee attrition (\u20b944.35 fees vs. \u20b9-30.23 net P&L) and vulnerability to mid-morning liquidity whipsaws. Forensics indicate that the `0.45%` minimum stop-loss sits within normal 5-minute bid-ask noise for high-beta NSE large-caps like TATASTEEL and AXISBANK, while the `1.0R` breakeven trigger chokes winning trades into fee-adjusted losses before institutional follow-through materializes. To mitigate false breakouts and overcome brokerage drag, we are widening `min_sl_pct` to `0.58%` to survive standard post-sweep retests, increasing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to `2.35x` to filter out low-conviction morning traps, shifting `breakeven_trigger_r` to `1.25R` to ensure locked-in stops comfortably cover round-trip statutory charges, and expanding `min_target_pct` to `1.40%` to restore positive expectancy."
